Validation suite of the UMD package

Runs the scripts of src/ on reference files and compares their results with those of a reference run, so that a change of the package
(a correction, a new option, the CPU parallelization of 3.0) shows every result it changes.

    python3 validation/run_validation.py            the default cases (about 15 minutes)
    python3 validation/run_validation.py --full     also the cases on the largest files
    python3 validation/run_validation.py -c 'workflow_*,parse_abinit'      some cases (names or patterns)
    python3 validation/run_validation.py -l         lists the cases
    python3 validation/run_validation.py --update   writes the results as the new reference (when a change is understood and wanted)

The C libraries must be compiled first (README.txt). The reference files are those of data/ (not distributed : about 2 GB of real runs) ;
-d gives another folder with the same files.

Each case runs in a fresh folder of its own (validation/runs/<date-time>/<case>/, not tracked ; -o another run folder), with links to
its inputs (zip files are extracted there) : data/ is never written to, and it is checked before and after the run. The output of each
command is in <nn>.<script>.out of the case folder ; report.txt sums up the run.

For each case the reference (reference/<case>.json, committed with the package) holds :
  - key numbers read from the output files by probes.py (density, P, T, E, Cv, cutoffs and coordination numbers, D, viscosity,
    S_2PT, species, results of the checks, statuses of the workflow steps...), compared within a relative tolerance (1e-4 by
    default : the last printed digit may change when sums are done in another order) ;
  - a checksum of every output file (dates and the path of the run folder left out ; figures and logs not compared) ;
  - the time of every command (differences above 30 % are listed, for information).

Status of a case :
  OK        every output identical to the reference
  CHANGED   some outputs differ, every key number within its tolerance (e.g. the last digit) : look at the files listed
  FAIL      a key number out of its tolerance or missing, or an output file not written
  CRASH     a command ended with an error code or printed a Python traceback (also in the logs of the workflow)
  NEW       no reference yet

cases.py   the cases : inputs, commands, probes
probes.py  readers of the output files, independent of the package
